ut like  this is like very nuanced it's very  challenging to like make that perfect so  would you say that you've been bit by  the acting bug now would you want to  maybe move on to a live-action role next  I don't know I'm still very camera shy  but at the same time I loved like drama  and theatre growing up I was always in  in theatre so we'll see I don't know I  do enjoy it but I have to like get more  comfortable I think let's say someone  else out there is about to jump into  their very first voice acting role after  having this experience what one major  tip would you give them to help them get  through it um I would say don't be shy  just like if you want to scream a lot  to scream it just don't be afraid of  sounding dumb or looking dumb like who  cares just go for it cuz at the end of  the day it's what the character needs  you know it's not even about you do you  remember the part in this process that  first made you do that did you have kind  of a breakthrough moment where you  finally I don't know kind of just went  for and acted silly and then you felt  good about it going forward yeah  definitely there are so many times where  Christians like just ad-lib apart here  just say what you feel and he would just  kind of hand off the floor to me and I  just remember like making up stuff and  just like screaming and just doing  different things and that was really  helpful just to get stuff out cuz you  really just remember that it's not you  it's you're lending your voice of  someone else and the second you like  stop worrying about it like looking down  then it you give so much more well job  well done I'm glad you learned able to  jump into it and get silly because this  movie is colorful vibrant and it's just  wacky in the best sense so  congratulations thank you thank you so  much
 

